.TH CLOG_GET_LEVEL 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
clog_get_level \- return the current minimum log level
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <clogger.h>

clog_level_t clog_get_level(clog logger);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns the current minimum severity level of the logger.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
logger  Logger handle.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Current minimum level.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Thread-safe: the minimum level is a per-logger, atomically updated
value, independent of the lock that serialises writes/rotation for
the shared output target, so reading one logger's level never
contends with a write in progress on a sibling logger sharing the
same target.
Asserts if logger is CLOG_INVALID, stale, or already closed.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clog_set_level (3)
